12. update preserves non-target indices;
13. map preserves length;
14. fold empty identity;
15. fold cons step;
16. replicate length;
17. replicate entry equality;
18. slice length;
19. slice entry correctness;
20. slice bounds;
21. vector length predicate correctness;
22. same-length reflexivity;
23. same-length symmetry;
24. same-length transitivity;
25. vector map entrywise correctness;
26. vector zip entrywise correctness;
27. finite sum empty zero;
28. finite sum cons step;
29. finite sum append additivity.

Section 5: Bytes, nibbles, hex digits, and little-endian encoding

Define byte as bounded u8, byte sequences, high nibble, low nibble, lowercase hex alphabet, u32 little-endian encoding, u64 little-endian encoding, and decoding.

Prove individually:

1. byte is u8;
2. byte bounds;
3. high nibble is in 0..15;
4. low nibble is in 0..15;
