8. little-endian u32 entries are bytes;
9. little-endian u64 entries are bytes;
10. little-endian u32 deterministic;
11. little-endian u64 deterministic;
12. little-endian u32 roundtrip;
13. little-endian u64 roundtrip;
14. byte-sequence append length;
15. prefix correctness;
16. suffix correctness.

Section 6: Real numeric semantics

Define real values, finite real predicate, `f32` semantic values, `f16` semantic values, addition, subtraction, multiplication, division, negation, absolute value, maximum, comparison, clipping, square root, exponential, tolerance comparison, derivative gate, f32 bit-pattern abstraction, f16 maximum, and f16 convertibility.

Do not replace floating-point behavior with integers. Do not define finiteness as always true unless the full semantic model justifies it. Do not use a fake exponentiation function.

Prove individually:

