33. derivative gate active at lower boundary;
34. derivative gate active at upper boundary;
35. derivative gate active inside interval;
36. f32 bits roundtrip real to bits to real;
37. f32 bits roundtrip bits to real to bits;
38. f16 convertibility implies finiteness;
39. f16 convertibility implies absolute-value bound.

Section 7: Shapes and tensors

Define shapes as finite sequences of natural dimensions. Define rank, rows, columns, expected length, 2D shape predicate, tensor structure with shape and data, valid 2D tensor predicate, tensor shape predicate, same-shape predicate, finite tensor predicate, row-major indexing, flat zero-based index, flat one-based index, tensor entry, row slice, and tensor equality.

Prove individually:

