13. same-shape implies same rows;
14. same-shape implies same columns;
15. tensor shape selector correctness;
16. tensor data selector correctness;
17. valid 2D iff rank two and expected data length;
18. valid 2D implies rank two;
19. valid 2D implies expected data length;
20. valid 2D implies rows defined;
21. valid 2D implies columns defined;
22. tensor-has-shape exact characterization;
23. tensor-has-shape implies rows;
24. tensor-has-shape implies columns;
25. tensor-has-shape implies data length;
26. tensors-same-shape reflexivity;
27. tensors-same-shape symmetry;
28. tensors-same-shape transitivity;
29. tensors-same-shape implies equal rows;
30. tensors-same-shape implies equal columns;
31. zero-based linear index formula;
32. one-based linear index formula;
33. linear index bounds;
34. tensor entry defined for valid indices;
35. tensor entry matches flat data;
36. tensor row slice length equals columns;
37. tensor row slice entry correctness;
38. tensor row slice bounds;
39. finite tensor all entries finite;
40. tensor equality iff shape and data equality;
41. data-length mismatch error;
42. shape mismatch error.

Section 8: Storage identity and aliasing

Define storage id, storage start, storage length, storage end, storage range, buffer identity, tensor buffer identity, tensor buffer start, tensor buffer length, tensor overlap, and aliasing.

Prove individually:

1. empty storage does not overlap on left;
2. empty storage does not overlap on right;
3. overlap symmetry;
4. disjoint storage ids imply no overlap;
5. same storage id may overlap when ranges intersect;
6. nonempty storage start is less than end;
7. no overlap if one end is before the other start;
8. overlap if ranges intersect;
9. tensor buffer overlap iff storage ranges overlap;
10. alias rejection returns `AliasedBuffers`;
11. non-overlap permits pair operation;
12. overlap behavior is deterministic.

Section 9: Checked arithmetic

Define exact checked arithmetic corresponding to the Zig file:

1. checked multiplication for `usize`;
2. checked multiplication for `u64`;
3. checked addition for `u64`;
4. checked cast from `u64` to `usize`.

Prove individually:

1. `checked_mul_usize` succeeds iff product is within `USIZE_MAX`;
2. `checked_mul_usize` fails iff product exceeds `USIZE_MAX`;
3. successful `checked_mul_usize` returns exact product;
4. failed `checked_mul_usize` returns `Overflow`;
5. `checked_mul_usize` deterministic;
6. `checked_mul_u64` succeeds iff product is within `U64_MAX`;
7. `checked_mul_u64` fails iff product exceeds `U64_MAX`;
8. successful `checked_mul_u64` returns exact product;
9. failed `checked_mul_u64` returns `Overflow`;
10. `checked_mul_u64` deterministic;
11. `checked_add_u64` succeeds iff sum is within `U64_MAX`;
12. `checked_add_u64` fails iff sum exceeds `U64_MAX`;
13. successful `checked_add_u64` returns exact sum;
14. failed `checked_add_u64` returns `Overflow`;
15. `checked_add_u64` deterministic;
16. cast succeeds iff value is within `USIZE_MAX`;
17. cast fails iff value is greater than `USIZE_MAX`;
18. successful cast returns exact value;
19. failed cast returns `TooLarge`;
20. cast deterministic;
21. dimension times dimension check prevents weight size overflow;
22. dimension times two check prevents model width overflow;
23. batch times dimension check prevents row traversal overflow;
24. rows times columns check prevents tensor read overflow.

Section 10: Validation layer

Define every validation function in the source file exactly, including clip range validation, comparison tolerance validation, tensor 2D validation, tensor exact-shape validation, finite-slice validation, model config validation, pair validation, metadata validation, and f16-convertibility validation.

Prove individually:

1. clip-range validation succeeds iff clip range is valid;
2. nonfinite clip minimum returns `NonFinite`;
3. nonfinite clip maximum returns `NonFinite`;
4. clip minimum not less than maximum returns `InvalidConfig`;
5. clip minimum below -20 returns `InvalidConfig`;
6. clip maximum above 20 returns `InvalidConfig`;
7. default clip range succeeds;
8. tolerance validation succeeds iff tolerances are valid;
9. nonfinite absolute tolerance returns `InvalidTolerance`;
10. nonfinite relative tolerance returns `InvalidTolerance`;
11. negative absolute tolerance returns `InvalidTolerance`;
12. negative relative tolerance returns `InvalidTolerance`;
13. tensor 2D validation succeeds iff tensor is valid 2D;
14. tensor rank mismatch returns `ShapeMismatch`;
15. tensor data-length mismatch returns `DataLengthMismatch`;
16. tensor exact-shape validation succeeds iff exact shape holds;
