Section 15: Scale-row semantics

Define scale-row computation exactly:

`pre_sum[d] = s_bias[d] + sum over j from 0 to dim-1 of s_weight[d,j] * input[j]`.

`clipped[d] = clip_min` if pre-sum is less than clip minimum.

`clipped[d] = clip_max` if pre-sum is greater than clip maximum.

`clipped[d] = pre_sum[d]` otherwise.

`scale[d] = exp(clipped[d])`.

Prove individually:

1. pre-sum definition;
2. scale row length equals dimension;
3. pre-sum entry formula;
4. below-clip case;
5. above-clip case;
6. inside-clip case;
7. scale entry formula;
8. scale values positive;
